# Featured Projects

A selection of open-source software, research tools, and computational systems I have designed and developed.

## 1. Static Content Engine for Researchers
A modular, zero-dependency Markdown reader designed to deploy academic portfolios instantly to static hosts like GitHub Pages.

- **Technologies:** HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+), Marked.js
- **Key Features:** Custom CSS variable themes, hash-based client routing, fully responsive layout.
- **Links:** [Repository](https://github.com) | [Live Demo](https://github.io)

---

## 2. Interactive Data Pipeline Visualizer
An open-source web application for rendering complex computational graphs into interactive, accessible visual representations.

- **Technologies:** Python, WebGL, Web Components
- **Key Features:** High-throughput node parsing, exportable SVG graphs, screen-reader support.
- **Links:** [Documentation](https://github.com) | [Paper](https://doi.org)

---

## 3. Accessible Courseware Template
An ultra-accessible static website template built for university instructors to publish syllabi, lecture slides, and assignment details.

- **Technologies:** Semantic HTML, Responsive Web Design, ARIA standards
- **Impact:** Adopted across 6 university departments serving 1,200+ enrolled students.
- **Links:** [Source Code](https://github.com)
